hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17369","Haddathana Abu Bakr al-Hanafi, he said haddathana Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar, from his father, from a man of Muzaynah, that his mother said to him: Will you not go and ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as people ask him. So I went to ask him, and I found him standing addressing, saying: Whoever abstains, Allah will make him chaste, and whoever enriches himself, Allah will enrich him, and whoever asks people while he has the worth of five ounces has asked importunately. So I said between me and myself: A she-camel of his is better than five ounces, and for his boy another she-camel better than five ounces, so I returned and did not ask him."
"17370","Haddathana Rawh, haddathana Zamah ibn Salih, he said I heard Ibn Shihab narrating that Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf informed him, from Abu Umamah Asad ibn Zurarah, and he was one of the chiefs on the day of al-Aqabah, that a thorn befell him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to visit him and said: A bad dead man for the Jews, twice, they will say: Why did he not defend his companion, and I own for him neither harm nor benefit, but I will strive for him. So he ordered him and he was cauterized with two lines above his head, then he died."
